From 7ab9bc8928bfe4dbfd7af70a2cc1dac44b97ca8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marek Jalovec <marek.jalovec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PMF: Do not use optional PMF if the driver does not support
 BIP

wpas_get_ssid_pmf() already ignores the pmf=1 default when the driver
does not support BIP, since the connection with PMF would fail. A network
profile with ieee80211w=1 was not covered, so wpa_supplicant enabled PMF
with an MFP-capable AP and the connection failed.

ConnMan sets ieee80211w=1 for WPA2/WPA3-Personal transition mode networks,
so devices whose driver does not support BIP (e.g., rtl8821cs) could not
connect to these networks at all.

Apply the same check to ieee80211w=1. PMF is optional for the network, so
connect without it instead of failing.

Signed-off-by: Marek Jalovec <marek.jalovec@gmail.com>
---
 wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
index 911d79d..a508442 100644
--- a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
@@ -7007,6 +7007,16 @@ int wpas_get_ssid_pmf(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s, struct wpa_ssid *ssid)
 		return wpa_s->conf->pmf;
 	}
 
+	if (ssid->ieee80211w == MGMT_FRAME_PROTECTION_OPTIONAL &&
+	    !(wpa_s->drv_enc & WPA_DRIVER_CAPA_ENC_BIP)) {
+		/*
+		 * Driver does not support BIP -- connect without PMF since the
+		 * connection with PMF would fail and the network does not
+		 * require it.
+		 */
+		return NO_MGMT_FRAME_PROTECTION;
+	}
+
 	return ssid->ieee80211w;
 #else /* CONFIG_IEEE80211W */
 	return NO_MGMT_FRAME_PROTECTION;
